  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/160919119/0.162.0</id>
    <updated>2026-10-23T18:47:17Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/releases/tag/0.162.0"/>
    <title>0.162.0</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Omitted &lt;code&gt;bool&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;bool | None&lt;/code&gt; form fields now use their declared defaults or produce missing-field errors, consistent with other fields and Pydantic behavior. FastAPI no longer infers &lt;code&gt;False&lt;/code&gt; for omitted booleans. This applies to individual form parameters, form models, and unions of form models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Omitted boolean model fields are excluded from &lt;code&gt;model_dump(exclude_unset=True)&lt;/code&gt;, and their defaults no longer count as submitted fields during union selection. Default factories and &lt;code&gt;validate_default&lt;/code&gt; follow the usual rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For HTML checkboxes, declare a boolean with a default of &lt;code&gt;False&lt;/code&gt;. See &lt;a href=&quot;https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/request-forms/#boolean-form-fields&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Boolean Form Fields&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Breaking Changes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🐛 Restore default handling for omitted boolean form fields. PR &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16605&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16605/hovercard&quot;&gt;#16605&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tiangolo&quot;&gt;@tiangolo&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</content>
